# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Student source material — DO NOT COMMIT
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# images/ holds photos of a child's schoolwork, including a
# Renaissance Star Reading progress report with her full name,
# school, teacher, and test scores. That is a minor's personally
# identifiable educational record. It must not go into version
# control — not even a private repo, since clones and forks carry
# it and history is hard to scrub after the fact.
images/

# Catch-all for photos dropped anywhere in the project. The apps
# use emoji and inline SVG, so a real photo here is almost always
# source material rather than something the site needs.
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.heic
*.gif
*.mp4
*.mov
*.pdf

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Superseded originals — kept locally, not pushed
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# bak/ holds older versions of files that have since been replaced
# (the standalone korean.html, the grade 5-6-only math generator).
# Useful on this machine for reference and for re-checking the data
# migration, but there is no reason to carry dead code in the repo.
# See bak/README.md for what each file was replaced by.
bak/

# apps/ contains only a redirect stub pointing at the live
# korean.html, and can be deleted.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build artifacts — regenerated by ./build/build.sh
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are large, machine-written, and rewritten wholesale on every
# build, which makes for noisy diffs and pointless merge conflicts.
# The authored sources they come from ARE committed:
#   math_questions.json  <- gen_math_grades.py
#   words_g56.json       <- words_a.json + words_b.json
#   spelling_words.json  <- words_g34 + words_g56 + words_g78
# Verified: deleting all three and running build.sh reproduces both
# app files byte-for-byte.
build/math_questions.json
build/spelling_words.json
build/words_g56.json

# NOTE: the built apps themselves (panda-math.html, spelling-bee.html)
# ARE committed on purpose. They are the deliverable — someone who
# clones this should be able to open index.html and use it without
# installing Python or Node.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dependencies
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
# build/package-lock.json is committed on purpose so test runs are
# reproducible — it pins the exact jsdom version the suites were
# written against.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets — nothing here uses them today, but cheap insurance
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.keystore
secrets.json
credentials.json
.netrc

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editors and tooling
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.\#*
\#*\#
.claude/
.aider*

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OS clutter
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Scratch
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.bak
*.bak.html
*.orig
*.rej
*.tmp
*.log
peek_*
.__deltest
/tmp/
